	abstract = {Contends that the location of the foci of green and blue in the perceptual Munsell color solid indicates that there is space for a derived color term between these 2 hues. Diachronic and synchronic linguistic studies on color term lexica are reviewed to explain why a term for turquoise is likely to develop into a derived basic color term in the languages of industrialized countries. A. C. Zimmer's (1982) hypothesis that türkis (in German) is the result of a universal production system for color terms is examined. Cultural, social, and psychological factors that influence the evolution of new basic color terms are described. (31 ref) (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)},
